flowchart How the searcher reads a file
// From: crates/searcher/src/searcher/mod.rs:643-720,727-767,769-790; crates/searcher/src/searcher/glue.rs:11-52,97-131; crates/core/flags/hiargs.rs:222-248
direction-tb

(search_path) -> [Open the file]
[Open the file] -> <Memory map enabled and opens?>
<Memory map enabled and opens?> -yes-> [[search_slice]]
<Memory map enabled and opens?> -no-> <File needs multi-line search?>
<File needs multi-line search?> -yes-> [Read the whole file onto the heap]
<File needs multi-line search?> -no-> [[search_reader]]
[Read the whole file onto the heap] -> [[MultiLine run]]
[[search_reader]] -> [Decode with encoding_rs]
[Decode with encoding_rs] -> <Reader needs multi-line search?>
<Reader needs multi-line search?> -yes-> [Read everything onto the heap]
<Reader needs multi-line search?> -no-> [[ReadByLine run]]
[Read everything onto the heap] -> [[MultiLine run]]
[[search_slice]] -> <Slice needs transcoding?>
<Slice needs transcoding?> -yes-> [[search_reader]]
<Slice needs transcoding?> -no-> <Slice needs multi-line search?>
<Slice needs multi-line search?> -yes-> [[MultiLine run]]
<Slice needs multi-line search?> -no-> [[SliceByLine run]]

note "Open the file" mod.rs:655 File::open
note "Memory map enabled and opens?" mod.rs:689 mmap.open, enabled only for 10 file paths or fewer unless asked, hiargs.rs:236
note search_slice mod.rs:769
note search_reader mod.rs:727
note "MultiLine run" glue.rs:166
note "ReadByLine run" glue.rs:38 rolls a line buffer
note "SliceByLine run" glue.rs:117 the fastest path
